From ee08173ae65876e7ba04f176fcb457c44178a042 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:28:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Compose held notifier selection with update
 checkpoints

Rebase onto main 65e18f963a (Park native gateway turns at durable update
boundaries). A started update checkpoint keeps precedence; only queued
selection skips notifier wakes held by a core-update drain. The started
checkpoint identity (attempted) and the validated queued selection stay
distinct, so checkpoint refusal and admission-conflict refusal each keep
their exact identity.

Fix review finding (t_01a1ce25bf75fb4a): when the selected head conflicts
and a cancel settles it during the async preclaim check, the drain now
re-reads and runs the follower instead of pausing admission_conflict with
the follower stranded queued.

Tests: new test_conflict_cancel_successor (RED with the fix reverted:
follower left queued; GREEN after), test_notifier_checkpoint_precedence,
and test_update_pause_refusal stubs forward the selection argument (no
assertion changes). Focused 36 files 271 passed; wider authority/claim/
wake/checkpoint sweep 96 files 488 passed, 4 skipped.
